-- The window for zoom.slap.
-- Run with: cat examples/zoom.slap examples/zoom-sdl.slap | ./slap-sdl
--
-- tick draws the whole canvas, so show has nothing to do. The image is W by H
-- and fills the largest aspect-preserving rectangle of the window, centered.
-- Each source pixel is one fill-rect, so the call count does not depend on the
-- window size. The model is the zoom state and a record of the canvas size.

start {'w 0 'h 0}

('rh let 'rw let rw 'w into rh 'h into) 'resize on

('t let 'g let
  g 'w at 'cw let  g 'h at 'ch let
  cw H mul ch W mul lt 'wide let
  wide (cw) (ch W mul H div) if 'tw let
  wide (cw H mul W div) (ch) if 'th let
  cw tw sub 2 div 'ox let
  ch th sub 2 div 'oy let
  -- per axis: where each source pixel's rectangle starts, and how long it is
  0 W range ('i let i tw mul W div ox plus) each 'X0 let
  0 W range ('i let i 1 plus tw mul W div i tw mul W div sub 1 max) each 'XW let
  0 H range ('i let i th mul H div oy plus) each 'Y0 let
  0 H range ('i let i 1 plus th mul H div i th mul H div sub 1 max) each 'YW let
  -- a canvas with no area shows nothing, so step runs without the draw calls
  tw 1 lt th 1 lt or (t (drop drop drop) step) (t (
    'lv let 'y let
    dup 'X0 nth must swap 'XW nth must
    y 'Y0 nth must swap y 'YW nth must
    lv fill-rect
  ) step) if g) 'tick on
(drop) show
